    },
    {
      "text": "\n\nWe want to extend a massive thank you to everyone who took part in this year’s Smaler's Charity Match, which raised an incredible £1,303!\nThe annual September match is held in memory of Dan Smale, a lifelong Leeds United fan and local footballer who sadly died of bowel cancer in 2019 at just 36. This marks the third year of raising funds for MUG in Dan’s memory, bringing the total raised to over £4,000!\nA huge thanks goes out to Manzur Gentlemens Hairdressers, Vale Recreation FC, the match officials, the organising committee, and everyone who came along to support, play, and donate.\nYour incredible support helps us continue raising awareness and supporting those affected by male cancers in Guernsey! See less",
      "date": "",
      "permalink": null,
      "hasVideo": false,
